@startuml domain-model-excerpt-us042
title Domain Model Excerpt Relevant to US042 (Import Bulk Weather Data)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classBackgroundColor #D6EAF8
skinparam classBorderColor      #5B9BD5
skinparam classFontColor        #1A1A1A
skinparam packageStyle           rectangle
skinparam packageBackgroundColor transparent
skinparam packageBorderColor     #888888
skinparam defaultFontSize        11
hide empty members

skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor<<external>> #EAEDED
    BorderColor<<external>>     #95A5A6
    FontColor<<external>>       #1A1A1A
    BackgroundColor<<new>>      #D5F5E3
    BorderColor<<new>>          #58D68D
}

' ============================================================
' AGGREGATE: WeatherData (reused from US041)
' US042 introduces NO new aggregate. It bulk-loads the SAME
' WeatherData aggregate US041 registers one record at a time.
' Classes tagged <<new>> are the deltas the mandatory sample
' file forces onto the existing US041 model (see readme 3.3).
' ============================================================
package "WeatherData Aggregate" {
    class WeatherData <<aggregate root>> {
        temperature  [optional]
        atmosphericPressure  [optional]
        visibility  [optional]
    }
    class WeatherDataId <<value object>>

    class TimePeriod <<value object>> {
        startTime
        endTime
    }

    class WeatherZone <<value object>> <<new>>
    class AltitudeBand <<value object>> <<new>> {
        lowerFeet
        upperFeet
    }
    class Coordinates <<value object>> {
        latitude
        longitude
    }

    class WeatherWindSpeed <<value object>>
    class WeatherWindDirection <<value object>>
    class DataSource <<value object>>

    WeatherData *-- WeatherDataId
    WeatherData *-- TimePeriod
    WeatherData *-- WeatherZone
    WeatherData *-- WeatherWindSpeed
    WeatherData *-- WeatherWindDirection
    WeatherData *-- DataSource

    WeatherZone *-- AltitudeBand
    WeatherZone *-- "2" Coordinates : SW, NE
}

note top of Coordinates
  Same VO type reused from the
  AirControlArea aggregate (no duplication).
  The instance belongs to WeatherData.
end note

' ============================================================
' EXTERNAL AGGREGATE (reference only, grey)
' The target area is selected at import time and must already
' exist. WeatherData references it root-to-root, by identity
' (AreaCode); no internal of either aggregate crosses the
' boundary.
' ============================================================
package "AirControlArea Aggregate" #EEEEEE {
    class AirControlArea <<aggregate root>> <<external>>
}

WeatherData --> AirControlArea : for area (by AreaCode, must exist)

note bottom of WeatherData
  No uniqueness invariant on
  (area, zone, band, period):
  multiple providers (DataSource)
  may forecast the same area+time,
  proven by the CW vs HP samples.
end note

@enduml